// {2}{G} 3/2: "When this creature enters, it fights target creature you
// don't control." — the fight family's SINGLE-target shape ([CR#701.14a]).
// Calibration evidence ([[cards-corpus-dry-run]]): even with only ONE
// announced target, spelling the fight's patient as `It` trips the strict R2
// gate HERE, because the enclosing ETB event's object is a second in-scope
// singular antecedent (`It reaches 2 antecedents`) — and both candidates are
// exact-sort creatures, so the pre-approved exact-sort-precedence loosening
// would not rescue it either. The sunset's answer
// ([[cards-fidelity-target-sunset]]) is the announce-list label: `As` names
// the slot and `The` reads it ([CR#608.2d]), leaving the frozen gate
// untouched — this fixture pins the announce-ambiguous shape's spelling.
Normal(
    name: "Creature ETB Fight One Target",
    mana_cost: [Generic(2), Green],
    types: [Creature],
    power: 3,
    toughness: 2,
    abilities: [
        Triggered(
            event: ThisEnters,
            effect: Targeted(
                targets: [As("target", TargetOne(AllOf([Creature, Not(ControlledBy(Ref(You)))])))],
                effect: Fight(This, The("target")),
            ),
        ),
    ],
)
